This is a faceless cinematic journey in a fixed five-beat format (POV sprint + body-slam through the door, POV brisk walk across the first room to a straight staircase, POV CONTINUOUS DESCENT, OFF-POV lateral tracking in the lower room, OFF-POV follow into another room). Honor the camera mode of this scene: scenes 1-3 are first-person POV (body-cam, body never visible except S1 forearms occasionally in the bottom of frame); scenes 4-5 are calm off-POV third-person, traveler seen only from behind or in profile, face never shown, clothing locked across S4 and S5. The descent is always a normal short straight step staircase going down, structurally attached, in an enclosed stairwell. Keep the locked structure identity through the exterior portions. The image must advance the journey only a believable short step from the previous keyframe. No on-screen text, numbers, logos, or watermarks. Single continuous frame only.

motion.prompt_template:
{kling_prompt}

This is a faceless cinematic journey in a fixed five-beat format. Honor the camera mode stated for this scene. SCENES 1-3 FIRST-PERSON POV (body-cam/GoPro/handheld). Scene 1: BODY-CAM on a panicked sprinting runner FLEEING on a slightly non-linear path STRAIGHT AT the door (centered at 20–25m in K0) — EXTREME footstep bob, WORLD RUSHES PAST at sprint speed (~6–7 m/s, ground flies past beneath, terrain blurs at frame edges), per-stride SURGE-AND-SETTLE (camera lurches forward as foot pushes off, jolts down as foot lands), panicked panting breath, door remains the dominant focal point, brief 1–2 shoulder-glances backward, forearms occasionally and briefly at the bottom of frame (not exaggerated), AND at the end the runner BODY-SLAMS the door (body, not hand), the door YIELDS INWARD instantly (swings AWAY from the camera INTO the structure), and the runner BARGES THROUGH without slowing — clip ends INSIDE the first room mid-stride FACING INTO the room (interior dominates, doorway BEHIND camera). Scene 2: a hurried purposeful POV walk across the first room interior to the top of the descending staircase, reduced bob, camera FACING FORWARD INTO the room throughout (never turning back to the doorway), ending at the top looking DOWN. Scene 3: POV CONTINUOUS DESCENT down the staircase, camera STAYS POV start-to-end (NEVER lifts off the head, NEVER cuts, NEVER floats through stairs, NEVER passes through walls, NEVER has a wall open up), angled DOWNWARD watching steps roll past, per-step bob downward, warm amber light grows brighter, ending at the bottom step or just stepping off. SCENES 4-5 OFF-POV THIRD-PERSON: calm controlled motion. Scene 4: a slow horizontal lateral tracking shot in the lower room while the traveler walks IN the room in ONE consistent forward direction (NOT on the staircase — staircase is a subtle edge element with higher steps cut off); interior locked, person appearance locked. Scene 5: a smooth continuous follow from behind as the traveler walks through into another luxurious room.

Keep the locked structure identity through the exterior portions. Advance the journey only a believable short distance per clip. The descent is always a normal short straight step staircase going DOWN, structurally attached. The stairwell is fully enclosed with no outdoor window. Any handrail is on the side wall only. The audio is natural diegetic sound only that matches the action exactly — wind/sea/rain + HARD pounding footsteps on the SPECIFIC ground surface and panicked panting breath (S1, + body-slam thud and door creak at end), brisk footsteps on the SPECIFIC first-room floor material (S2), footsteps descending the SPECIFIC stair material (S3), calm walking footsteps on the SPECIFIC lower-room floor material (S4-S5) — absolutely NO music. Every clip must depict ONE continuous motion from start to end — no time jumps, no mid-clip cuts, no skipping, no pauses, no floating through walls, no walls opening up; in S4 and S5 the person walks in ONE consistent direction without turning, reversing, walking backwards, melting, or changing appearance.
